# FI TUNE 2.0.0 is here

FI TUNE 2.0.0 brings a refreshed listening experience, with improvements across playback, appearance, and the player.

- **Playback recovery:** The app can try alternate supported stream clients and uses bounded retries for known failures. This can reduce playback interruptions, though stream availability still depends on external providers and your network.
- **Optional glass styling:** Lightweight translucent surfaces and highlights are available across key areas. Turn the effect on or off in Appearance.
- **Refreshed branding:** The red-sun FI TUNE artwork now appears in the app icon and splash/about screens. The familiar FI mark remains in the header and media notification.
- **Wave-style custom AOD player:** The custom always-on display player has a smoothly updating, seekable wave progress bar and glass-styled controls.
- **Media notification polish:** Media controls now use improved transport classification, lock-screen visibility, and accent color.
- **Update checker:** Check for the latest FI TUNE release from Settings > Updates.

**Download [FI TUNE 2.0.0 from GitHub](https://github.com/ignite-1018/FI-TUNE/releases/tag/V2.0.0).**

If you're on 1.0.4 and the in-app checker doesn't list 2.0.0, open the release link, download the APK, and install it over your existing FI TUNE app. The official 1.0.4 and 2.0.0 APKs use the same signing certificate, so you don't need to uninstall.

Android and device manufacturers control the appearance of the system lock screen and notification shade. FI TUNE's custom AOD styling appears in its own player screen.
